From: Phillip Blucas <pblucas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc: independent NAL slice threading (8.1.3 backport)

Based on FFmpeg PR23873 runtime commits d236db41faea7389c5130f250b5913a6bc15cabf
and5f8836c11e6040ab465c28c0a86b6fdfeae10b05. Original Signed-off-by:
Phillip Blucas <pblucas@gmail.com>. LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as the affected files.
Upstream proposal: https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23873
Retrieved proposal SHA256:078a4caaf2a7c40a2a11223eb619176f40b5c5435fc5834a353bd7c17fc1bd3b

Backport: retain8.1.3 weighted-bi DSP's separate offset arguments, replace
shared slice-header reads, and adapt WPP loop declarations/context lines.
No skipped luma/chroma filtering, reordered frames, bitstream or pixel changes.
Private strict output check by McFredward <frederik@lissek.info>: reject
missing reconstructed CTBs under AV_EF_EXPLODE before output. Valid decoded
pixels and all loop filters remain unchanged.

Private concurrency check by McFredward: keep the prefilled slice-address
table immutable during parallel jobs; retire incomplete ranges only after the
executor joins. Serial/WPP assignment remains unchanged.

Only the runtime changes from the proposal are included; app tests cover the
restricted authenticated Main8 mask contract independently.

